{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787261258628090002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"ruling-magnific-bats","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"ea6b46821952ba8cc9e99d02f9d4d5ddcdc38d0928037d61b7666ad48aa4a4bc","event_uuid":"24d12c22-7d2c-4d3d-ab5e-2915f5545a49","position":{"commit_sha":"9d4cae6cac527ed30c832efa572b31d0a596c566","position":"1787261235896009001-24d12c22-7d2c-4d3d-ab5e-2915f5545a49"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"1d943b5f71a027d21dadf307958d62475c33683dd2c13485bda9d4b7d38affc7","event_uuid":"d61123b2-cc94-49bd-8b25-d5b04fd0ba8d","position":{"commit_sha":"408fe940285e7715f6d8f4e7da281ec5ff8bbe23","position":"1787261253243285001-d61123b2-cc94-49bd-8b25-d5b04fd0ba8d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d77dc4ce6a3ffdce7c4160082969570bbfe84d8976b1d87dd10d8652cd64709d","event_uuid":"b8cde35b-c6cb-4de0-a158-d5fc239df6ab","position":{"commit_sha":"96fc438ed3ccb82c26529bfcc449717da4527898","position":"1787261258628090001-b8cde35b-c6cb-4de0-a158-d5fc239df6ab"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787261235896009001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d61123b2-cc94-49bd-8b25-d5b04fd0ba8d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"aa7b-5e47-6d3d-4615"}],"description":"## Problem\n\n`rebar transition <id> in_progress closed --caused-by=<origin>` **adds a `caused_by` edge without\nchecking whether an identical one already exists**, producing two distinct links to the same\ntarget. Since `caused_by` feeds `rebar metrics`' escape-rate lenses and the epic-close `caused_by`\nfloor, a duplicated edge double-counts one escaped defect as two.\n\n## Observed, twice, in one session\n\nBoth tickets had a `caused_by` link recorded earlier via `rebar link`, then were closed with the\nsame value passed explicitly as `--caused-by`:\n\n```\nirongrey-chubby-oxpecker  caused_by -> 789c-1251-fc21-4cf6   (x2)\nperkish-balsamic-pupfish  caused_by -> fc20-2df1-426e-42ab   (x2)\n```\n\nTwo DISTINCT links, same relation, same target:\n\n```\nlink_uuid= 4ae0ef85-aa7b-4ec8-9678-9dda3ee24133  target= 789c-1251-fc21-4cf6\nlink_uuid= be724547-5b94-417a-8e2c-aa5b32d994ea  target= 789c-1251-fc21-4cf6\n```\n\nA survey of the whole store found **exactly these two** tickets with duplicate `caused_by` edges,\nwhich is consistent with the trigger being rare in practice — most closes do one or the other, not\nboth.\n\n## The part that makes this worth fixing rather than just avoiding\n\n**The `/rebar-debug` protocol instructs you to do both things that combine to cause it.** From the\nattribution step:\n\n> Recording the link early with `rebar link <bug-id> <origin-id> caused_by` ... is fine and often\n> useful — it gets the finding down before Phase 2 can be interrupted — but it does **not** stand in\n> for the flag. A close with an empty `--caused-by` re-runs blame auto-derivation unconditionally;\n> it does not check whether the ticket already carries a `caused_by` edge, so it will happily add a\n> second, guessed edge *beside* your proven one. ... Pass the flag on the close every time.\n\nThat guidance is correct about the danger it names (an empty flag lets blame add a **wrong** edge),\nand following it faithfully — link early, then always pass the flag — deterministically produces a\n**duplicate** edge instead. The advice and the implementation together guarantee the defect for any\nagent that follows the protocol properly. Both tickets above were closed by exactly that route.\n\nSo the duplicate is not a user error to be documented away; it is the protocol's prescribed path.\n\n## Severity, stated honestly\n\nBounded. A duplicate edge points at the RIGHT origin, so it is strictly less harmful than the\nwrong-edge case the guidance was written to prevent — nothing is mis-attributed. The harm is\ndouble-counting in the metric, and `rebar unlink <source> <target> caused_by` repairs it after the\nfact (used successfully on both tickets above, including on already-CLOSED tickets). Filed P2 on\nthat basis rather than higher.\n\n## Reproduction\n\n1. Claim a bug and confirm an origin ticket for it.\n2. `rebar link <bug> <origin> caused_by`.\n3. Close it: `rebar transition <bug> in_progress closed --class=<class> --caused-by=<origin>`.\n4. `rebar show <bug>` — the `deps` list contains **two** `caused_by` entries with distinct\n   `link_uuid`s and the same `target_id`.\n\n## Direction (not a prescription)\n\nMaking the `--caused-by` write **idempotent** for an identical (relation, target) pair is the\nobvious candidate and would leave every other path unchanged. Worth checking whether the same\nnon-dedup applies to `rebar link` generally, or only to the close path's write — the two have\ndifferent call sites and the fix may belong in only one of them. A blanket dedup across all\nrelations would be a larger behavioural change and is NOT proposed here: `relates_to` and\n`discovered_from` may have legitimate reasons to permit repeats, and that question should be\nanswered on evidence rather than assumed.\n\nIf the code is left as-is, the alternative remedy is to correct the `/rebar-debug` guidance so it\nstops prescribing the combination — but that trades a clean invariant for a rule agents must\nremember, which is the weaker fix.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Closing a bug with `--caused-by=<origin>` when an identical `caused_by` edge already exists\n      leaves exactly ONE such edge — verified by a test driving the four-step reproduction above.\n- [ ] The protection the current guidance exists for is retained: closing with an EMPTY\n      `--caused-by` must still not silently add a competing guessed edge beside an existing proven\n      one — verified by a test.\n- [ ] A different origin passed via `--caused-by` when one is already recorded is NOT silently\n      dropped: it either replaces the existing edge or fails loudly. Decide which and test it —\n      silently ignoring a corrected attribution would be a worse bug than this one.\n- [ ] `rebar metrics`' escape-rate lens counts one escaped defect once for a ticket that went\n      through the link-then-flag path — verified against the reproduction.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n      (`new=0 increased=0 stale=0`) pass.\n\n## Provenance\n\nFound in live operation while closing `irongrey-chubby-oxpecker` and `perkish-balsamic-pupfish`\nunder `/rebar-debug`. Both were repaired with `rebar unlink` and now carry exactly one edge each, so\nno metric is currently skewed by them.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/transition_close.py","reason":"The close path writes the --caused-by edge without deduping against an identical existing (relation, target) pair."},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/close_disposition.py","reason":"Candidate home for the caused_by application/dedup, depending on where _apply_caused_by resolves."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_caused_by_dedup_10d0.py","reason":"New test driving the link-then-close reproduction and the empty-flag protection that must be retained."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"10d0-c26c-bdbb-4b1f","ticket_type":"bug","title":"close --caused-by adds a duplicate edge when an identical caused_by link already exists","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["24d12c22-7d2c-4d3d-ab5e-2915f5545a49","d61123b2-cc94-49bd-8b25-d5b04fd0ba8d","b8cde35b-c6cb-4de0-a158-d5fc239df6ab"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787261258628090002,"uuid":"f55ec491-0886-4ccd-b430-5df2306d0ea1"}